In article <HAIRSTON.90Jul21001452@henry.ece.cmu.edu>, hairston@henry.ece.cmu.edu (David Hairston) writes:
> hmmm, what i noticed one time while playing pl9 was that i
> came across a conical key.  i picked it up and _called_ it
> "connie".  a few moves later i stumble across:
> "a square key called connie".
> 
> this doesn't happen if the keys aren't skeleton ...

Most of the time it doesn't happen.

But let's say skeleton keys are triangular in your game.  Call it
skeleton (a triangular key called skeleton).  Now you come across a
ghost pile, where conical keys were skeleton keys.  You'll see "a
conical key called skeleton."

I've never actually picked one of those up to see if they actually do
work like skeleton keys, so it may be that it simply kept the name
from the previous game.

